{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-lam-1-intro","title":"Lamentations 1 — Chapter Introduction","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":0,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":0},"content":"<p>Thus shall. 42; 25:27; Na 1:8,9; Re 14:8; 18:2,21 they shall. 58; Hab 2:13; Ps 76:12 Thus far. Job 31:40; Ps 72:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-1","title":"Lamentations 1:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The miseries of Jerusalem and of the Jews pathetically lamented, with confessions of their sins. 12 The attention and compassion of beholders demanded to this unprecedented case. 18 The justice of God acknowledged, and his mercy supplicated, with prayers against insulting foes.</p>\n<p>How doth.The LXX. have the following words as an introduction: \"And it came to pass after Israel had been carried captive, and Jerusalem was become desolate, that Jeremiah sat weeping, and lamented with this lamentation over Jerusalem, and said.\"</p>\n<p>2:1; 4:1; Isa 14:12; Jer 50:23; Zep 2:15; Re 18:16,17 sit. 2:10; Isa 3:26; 47:1-15; 50:5; 52:2,7; Jer 9:11; Eze 26:16 full. Ps 122:4; Isa 22:2; Zec 8:4,5 as a. Isa 47:8,9; 54:4; Re 18:7 great. 1Ki 4:21; 2Ch 9:26; Ezr 4:20 how is. 5:16; 2Ki 23:33,35; Ne 5:4; 9:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-2","title":"Lamentations 1:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>weepeth. 16; 2:11,18,19; Job 7:3; Ps 6:6; 77:2-6; Jer 9:1,17-19; 13:17 among. 19; Jer 4:30; 22:20-22; 30:14; Eze 16:37; 23:22-25; Ho 2:7 Re 17:13,16 none. 9,16,17,21; Isa 51:18,19 all her friends. Job 6:15; 19:13,14; Ps 31:11; Pr 19:7; Mic 7:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-3","title":"Lamentations 1:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>gone. 2Ki 24:14,15; 25:11,21; 2Ch 36:20,21; Jer 39:9; 52:15,27-30 because of great servitude. Heb. for the greatness ofservitude. she. 2:9; Le 26:36-39; De 28:64-67; Jer 24:9; Eze 5:12 all. 4:18,19; Jer 16:16; 52:8; Am 9:1-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-4","title":"Lamentations 1:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>ways. 2:6,7; 5:13; Isa 24:4-6; Jer 14:2; Mic 3:12 all her gates. 2:9; Jer 9:11; 10:22; 33:10-12 her priests. 11,12,18-20; 2:10,11,19-21; Isa 32:9-14; Joe 1:8-13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-5","title":"Lamentations 1:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>adversaries. 2:17; 3:46; Le 26:17; De 28:43,44; Ps 80:6; 89:42; Isa 63:18 Jer 12:7; Mic 7:8-10 for. 18; 3:39-43; Le 26:15-46; De 4:25-27; 28:15-68; 29:18-28 De 31:16-18,29; 32:15-27; 2Ch 36:14-16; Ne 9:33,34; Ps 90:7,8 Jer 5:3-9,29; 23:14; 30:14,15; 44:21,22; Eze 8:17,18; 9:9; 22:24-31 Da 9:7-16; Mic 3:9-12; Zep 3:1-8 her children. Jer 39:9; 52:27-30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-6","title":"Lamentations 1:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>from. 2Ki 19:21; Ps 48:2,3; Isa 1:21; 4:5; 12:6; Zep 3:14-17 all. 2:1-7; 2Sa 4:11,12; Ps 50:2; 96:9; 132:12,13; Jer 52:8,11,13 Eze 7:20-22; 11:22,23; 24:21,25 her princes. Le 26:36,37; De 28:25; 32:30; Jos 7:12,13; Ps 44:9-11; Jer 29:4 Jer 48:41; 51:30-32; 52:7 harts. Jer 14:5,6; 47:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-7","title":"Lamentations 1:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>remembered. Job 29:2-25; 30:1; Ps 42:4; 77:3,5-9; Ho 2:7; Lu 15:17; 16:25 all her. De 4:7,8,34-37; 8:7-9; Ps 147:19,20; Isa 5:1-4 pleasant. or, desirable. 10 the adversaries. 2:15,16; Ps 79:4; 137:3,4; Mic 4:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-8","title":"Lamentations 1:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>hath. 5,20; 1Ki 8:46,47; 9:7,9; Isa 59:2-13; Jer 6:28; Eze 14:13-21 Eze 22:2-15 removed. Heb. become a removing, or wandering. Jer 15:4; 24:9; 34:17; Eze 23:46; *marg: all. 4:15,16; 5:12-16; 1Sa 2:30 they. 4:21; Isa 47:3; Jer 13:22,26; Eze 16:37-39; 23:29; Ho 2:3,10 Re 3:18 she sigheth. 4,11,21,22; 2:10; Jer 4:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-9","title":"Lamentations 1:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>filthiness. 17; Jer 2:34; 13:27; Eze 24:12,13 she remembereth. De 32:29; Isa 47:7; Jer 5:31; 1Pe 4:17 came. 1; 4:1; Isa 3:8; Jer 13:17,18 she had. 2,17,21; 2:13; Ec 4:1; Isa 40:2; 54:11; Ho 2:14; Joh 11:19 behold. Ex 3:7,17; 4:31; De 26:7; 1Sa 1:11; 2Sa 16:12; 2Ki 14:26; Ne 9:32 Ps 25:18; 119:153; Da 9:17-19 for. De 32:27; Ps 74:8,9,22,23; 140:8; Isa 37:4,17,23,29; Jer 48:26 Jer 50:29; Zep 2:10; 2Th 2:4-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-10","title":"Lamentations 1:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>spread. 7; Isa 5:13,14; Jer 15:13; 20:5; 52:17-20 pleasant. or, desirable. 7 seen. Ps 74:4-8; 79:1-7; Isa 63:18; 64:10,11; Jer 51:51; 52:13; Eze 7:22 Eze 9:7 whom. De 23:3; Ne 13:1; Eze 44:7; Mr 13:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-11","title":"Lamentations 1:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>seek. 19; 2:12; 4:4-10; De 28:52-57; 2Ki 6:25; Jer 19:9; 38:9; 52:6 Eze 4:15-17; 5:16,17 relieve the soul. Heb. make the soul to come again. 1Sa 30:11,12 see. 9,20; 2:20; Job 40:4; Ps 25:15-19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-12","title":"Lamentations 1:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Is it nothing. or, It is nothing. pass by. Heb. pass bythe way. if. The church in distress here magnifies her affliction; and yet no more than there was cause for her groaning was not heavier than her strokes. She appeals to all spectators--see if there be any sorrow like unto my sorrow. This might truly be said of the griefs which were suffered in Jerusalem of old; but Christians are apt to apply these words too sensibly and sensitively to themselves, when they are in trouble, and sometimes more than there is reasonable cause to warrant. All men feel most from their own burden, and cannot be persuaded to reconcile themselves to it; how often do thy cry out in the words we are illustrating! whereas, if their troubles were to be thrown into a common stock with those of others, and then an equal dividend made, share and share alike, rather than approve such an arrangement, each would be ready to say, \"Pray give me my own again.\"--Henry.</p>\n<p>2:13; 4:6-11; Da 9:12; Mt 24:21; Lu 21:22,23; 23:28-31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-13","title":"Lamentations 1:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>above. 2:3,4; De 32:21-25; Job 30:30; Ps 22:14; 31:10; 102:3-5; Na 1:6 Hab 3:16; 2Th 1:8; Heb 12:29 he hath spread. 4:17-20; Job 18:8; 19:6; Ps 66:11; Eze 12:13; 17:20; 32:3; Ho 7:12 he hath turned. Ps 35:4; 70:2,3; 129:5; Isa 42:17 desolate. 22; 5:17; De 28:65; Jer 4:19-29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-14","title":"Lamentations 1:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>yoke. De 28:48; Pr 5:22; Isa 14:25; 47:6; Jer 27:8,12; 28:14 delivered. Jer 25:9; 34:20,21; 37:17; 39:1-9; Eze 11:9; 21:31; 23:28; 25:4,7 Ho 5:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-lam-1-15","title":"Lamentations 1:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LAM","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":15},"content":